<title>JAPAN: JT jumps on hopes for AIDS research.</title>
<headline>JT jumps on hopes for AIDS research.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Japan Tobacco Inc, which has developed an anti-viral therapy for HIV with Agouron Pharmaceuticals Inc, jumped on Monday afternoon on hopes that the upcoming G7 summit will encourage AIDS-related research, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0511 GMT, the shares were up 12,000 yen at 921,000, giving up some gains after briefly touching 924,000 yen, a new high for the calendar year.</p>
</text>
